meta {
  name: 20 - Projects Bare
  type: graphql
  seq: 20
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query ProjectsBare {
    projects(first: 2, includeArchived: true, sort: [{updatedAt: {order: Ascending}}]) {
      nodes {
        id
        createdAt
        updatedAt
        archivedAt
        name
        description
        slugId
        icon
        color
        health
        priority
        priorityLabel
        sortOrder
        prioritySortOrder
        startDate
        targetDate
        startedAt
        completedAt
        canceledAt
        autoArchivedAt
        healthUpdatedAt
        trashed
        progress
        scope
        url
        slackChannelId
        content
        status { id }
        creator { id }
        lead { id }
        leadTeam { id }
        lastAppliedTemplate { id }
        convertedFromIssue { id }
      }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/graphql

  The canonical Projects selection set — verbatim what the connector will send. Same
  construction rules as `10 - Issues Bare`: all cheap scalars, relations as `{ id }` only,
  and no nested connections (`issues`, `members`, `teams`, `projectUpdates`,
  `projectMilestones`, `documents`, `comments`, `history` are all deliberately omitted).

  Static cost under the documented formula (27 scalars, 6 relation objects): per node =
  1 + 27 x 0.1 + 6 x 1.1 = ~10.3 points; at `first: 250` that is ~2,575 points — roughly
  4x headroom under the 10,000-point cap, the roomiest of the four streams.

  Two scalars to keep an eye on: `content` (long-form project brief) and `progressHistory`
  / `currentProgress` (JSON blobs). `content` is included because it is genuine project
  data; the progress-history JSON scalars are OMITTED — they are large, high-churn
  derived aggregates, and they would bloat every document for little analytical value.

  `projects` accepts the `sort` argument (verified by introspection), so this stream uses
  the ascending `updatedAt` sweep and may checkpoint per page.

  **Limitation / observed finding — `identifier` is ENTITLEMENT-GATED and has been REMOVED
  from this selection set.** With the stream empty (2026-07-30) the field resolved without
  complaint. Once `Seeding/A1`/`A2` created a real record (2026-08-04), requesting it
  returned:

      HTTP 200
      "errors": [{ "extensions": { "code": "INPUT_ERROR" },
                   "message": "Feature 'Project IDs' is not enabled",
                   "path": ["projects","nodes",0,"identifier"] }]

  **and `data` was still populated** — the row came back intact, with the errors array
  alongside it. This is the third and nastiest variant of the "HTTP 200 does not mean
  success" rule in this collection: not a total failure (`06`, `data: null`) and not a
  clean rejection (`42`, HTTP 400), but a PARTIAL SUCCESS carrying both real data and a
  real error.

  Two lessons carried into the plan:

  1. **Entitlement-gated fields are a portability hazard unique to GraphQL selection sets.**
     REST returns whatever the plan allows; GraphQL returns only what you ask for, so asking
     for a field the workspace is not entitled to poisons every response — on every page,
     forever. `identifier` is a paid add-on ('Project IDs') and is not worth that: `id`, `slugId`
     and `url` already identify the record. Removed.
  2. **The connector's error handling must distinguish partial success from total failure.**
     Treating any non-empty `errors` array as fatal would break the sync outright on every
     workspace lacking this feature; ignoring `errors` would hide genuine failures. Branch
     on whether `data` is present.

  Only discoverable with data in the stream — the empty-endpoint run gave a false all-clear.

  **Limitation / observed finding — POPULATED as of 2026-08-04.** `Seeding/A1` created one
  project, so this stream now has a real observed response body (see the saved example):
  `status` resolves as an OBJECT `{id, name, type}`, `health` is null in practice, and
  `identifier` was stripped for the entitlement reason above. Field nullability, the
  `status` shape and cursor behavior are all now confirmed against live data rather than
  inferred from introspection.

  <!-- Historical, pre-seed (2026-07-30): -->
  **Superseded — this endpoint WAS empty.** The Estuary workspace contained
  ZERO projects, with or without `includeArchived: true` (confirmed 2026-07-30). The query
  is accepted and every field above resolves without error, which proves the selection set
  is VALID against the live schema — but no response body has ever been observed for this
  stream. Field nullability in practice, the real shape of `status`/`health`, and cursor
  behavior are all unobserved.

  Closing this gap requires `Seeding/A1 - Create Project`, which the user must run. Until
  then this stream's response shape rests on introspection alone.
}

example {
  name: 200 — populated Project (identifier removed: entitlement-gated)

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query ProjectsBare {
        projects(first: 2, includeArchived: true, sort: [{updatedAt: {order: Ascending}}]) {
          nodes {
            id
            createdAt
            updatedAt
            archivedAt
            name
            description
            slugId
            icon
            color
            health
            priority
            priorityLabel
            sortOrder
            prioritySortOrder
            startDate
            targetDate
            startedAt
            completedAt
            canceledAt
            autoArchivedAt
            healthUpdatedAt
            trashed
            progress
            scope
            url
            slackChannelId
            content
            status { id }
            creator { id }
            lead { id }
            leadTeam { id }
            lastAppliedTemplate { id }
            convertedFromIssue { id }
          }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 18
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2485
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2999975
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "projects": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "id": "1904e338-af08-4cbb-aacd-033e8845e3c0",
                  "createdAt": "2026-08-04T18:35:04.021Z",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:35:04.021Z",
                  "archivedAt": null,
                  "name": "estuary-connector-verification",
                  "description": "Temporary record created to verify source-linear Projects stream. Safe to delete.",
                  "slugId": "6beb53347968",
                  "icon": null,
                  "color": "#5e6ad2",
                  "health": null,
                  "priority": 0,
                  "priorityLabel": "No priority",
                  "sortOrder": -31,
                  "prioritySortOrder": -31,
                  "startDate": null,
                  "targetDate": null,
                  "startedAt": null,
                  "completedAt": null,
                  "canceledAt": null,
                  "autoArchivedAt": null,
                  "healthUpdatedAt": null,
                  "trashed": null,
                  "progress": 0,
                  "scope": 0,
                  "url": "https://linear.app/estuary-test/project/estuary-connector-verification-6beb53347968",
                  "slackChannelId": null,
                  "content": null,
                  "status": {
                    "id": "5c520723-dcc9-42d2-8127-5d759c43e256"
                  },
                  "creator": {
                    "id": "8ef0e033-440f-4809-b0ff-6a68821fc413"
                  },
                  "lead": null,
                  "leadTeam": null,
                  "lastAppliedTemplate": null,
                  "convertedFromIssue": null
                }
              ],
              "pageInfo": {
                "hasNextPage": false,
                "endCursor": "eyJrZXkiOiIxOTA0ZTMzOC1hZjA4LTRjYmItYWFjZC0wMzNlODg0NWUzYzAiLCJncm91cHMiOlsiIiwiIl19"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
